+## Plugin cvars (`cinecam_*`)
+
+Registered by the CinematicCamera plugin itself, not by the renderer. They are process-wide, so
+they are not tied to any one camera entity.
+
+### cinecam_LutHotReload
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Default | **30** in the editor, **0** in the launcher |
+| Purpose | Re-read the display chain's `.cube` files - the camera's **ODT File** and the CineCam Grade's **LMT File** - when they change on disk, every N frames. `0` = off. Author a look in Resolve on one monitor and watch the picture follow on the other. |
+| Mechanism | A poll of `(modification time, size)` through `ICryPak`, on the same two-tree search the loader used, so the watcher cannot end up watching a different file from the one in the picture. It is a poll and not the editor's `IFileChangeMonitor` because that interface exists only inside Sandbox *and* watches only the project tree - a cube installed into `<engine>/engine/Assets/ODT/` would never fire. |
+| Safety | A change has to be seen **twice** before it is acted on, so a half-written file is not loaded. A reload that fails to parse **keeps the previous good LUT** and warns once with the reason - the picture does not change under you when you did not ask for it. (A path you *type* that does not parse still clears the slot, deliberately: you must see that it is wrong.) |
